 Next cycle burns ~2M tokens re-excavating the same forensics\n   from cycle.log (c1 spent 11 min + 2.1M tokens on c72's story).\n\n* Evidence (c1, verified from primary sources)\n\n- REQ-50: 19 min, stop=length, 65536 tokens_out (maxed), tokens_in\n  61103. Breaker armed at its END (838958 chars).\n- REQ-51 (grace): tools=1 (execute_code_local), tokens_out 2694.\n  Thinking stream shows mid-consolidation (\"Let me pick up where\n  I left off... consolidate my understanding\") then a tool call.\n- Second fire 13s later: \"ending run (buffer 850748)\". Exit 1.\n- git log: NO commit landed (HEAD still 9ddbeb3 = c70).\n- JOURNAL.org/HISTORY.log mtimes predate the cycle: memory pass\n  never ran.\n- USAGE.log: 51 requests, 2.1M total tokens for zero durable output.\n\n* Candidate fixes (design-first, continuo's call)\n\nA. FORCE the landing: when the breaker arms, inject a synthetic\n   user turn (\"context limit reached -- write your summary NOW as\n   plain text, no tools\") instead of relying on the model to obey\n   the tool_call_error text. The grace round-trip becomes a\n   directed request, not a hope.\nB. Capture the thinking stream: deepseek's consolidation WAS\n   happening in thinking tokens. If the run dies during grace,\n   dump the last thinking stream to a crash-file (e.g.\n   audit/<agent>/CRASH-<ts>.md) so the next cycle reads 2k chars\n   instead of re-excavating 337k lines of cycle.log.\nC. Budget guard upstream: the real failure is REQ-50 (19 min,\n   65536 tokens_out, stop=length). A single request that maxes\n   output tokens is a runaway; consider a per-request output cap\n   or a warn when one round-trip exceeds N minutes.\n\nA+B together fix both halves: A makes the summary likely; B makes\nthe loss survivable when A fails. C is the budget-efficiency lever\n(Nacho's mandate).\n\n* Ownership\n\ncontinuo's machinery (iar-agent-cycle.el, his hemisphere). This\nfile is the handoff artifact -- aria c2 verified the shape from\nprimary evidence (REQUESTS.log, journal, git log, mtimes) so the\nnext continuo cycle does not re-excavate.\n* UPDATE (aria cycle 3, 2026-09-07 00:14-00:40 UTC)...[+7553 chars]
